    "number": 240,
    "title": "feat(#124): generate lint reference pages from registered lint set",
    "body": "## Description\n\nThis PR introduces a **single source of truth** for lint metadata by replacing the hand-maintained lint summary in \\docs/lints/README.md\\ with an auto-generated version. A new standalone generator crate (\\\tools/generate-lint-docs\\) parses the authoritative \\declare_lint!\\ blocks and \\LINT_METADATA\\ array in \\soroban_cost_lints/src/lib.rs\\ to produce both:\n\n- **\\docs/lints/README.md\\** — the human-readable lint reference table\n- **\\docs/lints/lint-registry.json\\** — a machine-readable registry consumable by \\#96\\ (\\--list-lints\\) and \\#103\\ (\\--explain\\)\n\n## Key design decisions\n\n- **Generator is a standalone binary** (\\\tools/generate-lint-docs\\) rather than a build script or test, so it can be run on demand and in CI without a full rustc build.\n- **Boundary**: only structured metadata (name, level, description, category) is generated. Per-lint prose pages remain hand-written — the generator reads descriptions from \\declare_lint!\\ blocks but never modifies the \\.md\\ doc pages.\n- **CI drift check**: \\.github/workflows/lint.yml\\ includes \\cargo run -p generate-lint-docs -- --check\\ which fails if the committed output differs from generated output.\n- **Machine-readable output**: \\lint-registry.json\\ exposes the full inventory in a shape that \\#96\\ and \\#103\\ can consume directly.\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Action |\n|------|--------|\n| \\\tools/generate-lint-docs/Cargo.toml\\ | Created |\n| \\\tools/generate-lint-docs/src/main.rs\\ | Created |\n| \\docs/lints/lint-registry.json\\ | Created |\n| \\Cargo.toml\\ (workspace) | Added \\\tools/generate-lint-docs\\ member |\n| \\.github/workflows/lint.yml\\ | Added CI drift check step |\n| \\CONTRIBUTING.md\\ | Replaced manual doc update instructions with regeneration command |\n| \\docs/lints/README.md\\ | Regenerated (now includes previously-missing \\host_in_loop\\ entry) |\n\n## Regeneration\n\nTo regenerate the docs after adding/modifying a lint:\n\n\\\\\\\bash\ncargo run -p generate-lint-docs\n\\\\\\\n\nCloses #124",
